[thin] Specific cosmetic-flute profile exception: these are true short chords across the exterior groove/land contour, including its aft-edge fade. All nineteen interior samples along each emitted pair contain material in the actual finished STL. The shared profile is 4 mm wide and 1.2 mm deep with a 5 mm smoothstep fade; current closed-field pitch is 5.0073 mm. The corner coupon and full-front photographs in cadlib/flute-evidence/README.md establish profile and appearance scopes. This is not a 3 mm structural-wall or exact current-field print-acceptance claim; deposition, finish and load capacity remain unqualified.
alternatives: Flattening or shallowing the grooves changes the retained visible profile. Widening lands changes the closed-field spacing. Either finish change needs its own appearance assessment; a through-thickness-only cutoff cannot choose the cosmetic profile.
