[sliver] Required by the purchased K&J SB443-IN's side grooves: each magnet column's slot is the printed capture Derek specified for these stepped blocks, faces touching, loaded at one print pause. The 1.575 mm faces seat each block's 1.6 mm front band from the flat back to its rails, the 1.500 mm faces are the rails' tips standing in the 1.6 mm grooves, and the 0.797 mm faces are the rails' fore and aft bearing faces, the groove's 0.787 mm depth plus the 0.1 mm side air less the 0.09 mm tip air. Each runs the slot's 26 mm. pump-dock/magnet-retention.md gives the slot.
alternatives: A wider or deeper rail does not enter the 1.6 × 0.79 mm groove. A cover across the pole face keeps the faces apart. Bonded blocks in plain pockets need DP420, two sequential 24 h cures and a seating fixture, which this capture replaces.
